<http://data.silknow.org/event/b759fa68-557d-3e0e-9f56-309e31ecfca7>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Purchased in 1890 from Fratelli Mora, 35 Solferino, Milan for £3 - 18 - 0\n\nComparable pairs of bellows in the V&amp;A collection are 1400-1904 (with figure of Love and the Four Elements), W.11-1930 (with figure of Plenty), and W.142-1921 (Berainesque decoration.)\n\nComparable bellows associated with the town of Spa survive in the Musées de la Ville d'eaux - Spa (SN12), and the Museum of the Walloon Life in Liège www.viewallonne.be - reflecting a decorative character dominated by the Principality of Liège."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6febcb53-022c-373d-8f36-58575ffa6a2d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Purchased in 1890 from Fratelli Mora, 35 Solferino, Milan for £3 - 18 - 0\n\nComparable pairs of bellows in the V&amp;A collection are 1400-1904 (with figure of Love and the Four Elements), W.11-1930 (with figure of Plenty), and W.142-1921 (Berainesque decoration.)\n\nComparable bellows associated with the town of Spa survive in the Musées de la Ville d'eaux - Spa (SN12), and the Museum of the Walloon Life in Liège www.viewallonne.be - reflecting a decorative character dominated by the Principality of Liège."@en .

